<title>CHINA: TRADING IN CHINA DEV SHARES SUSPENDED.</title>
<headline>TRADING IN CHINA DEV SHARES SUSPENDED.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of China Development Corp Ltd was suspended in late morning at the company's request pending an announcement, the Hong Kong Stock Exchange said on Friday.</p>
<p>Its shares rose HK$0.31 or 25.20 percent to HK$1.54 prior to the trading suspension. Volume was 21.73 million shares worth HK$32.82 million.</p>
<p>The company, formerly named Sum Cheong International Ltd, is involved in trading, construction, mining and manufacturing.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6370</p>
